  "notes": "A formal, technical word used in academic papers, textbooks, and presentations. Functions as a suru verb ({図示|ずし}する).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {図示|ずし}する — to illustrate, to show in a diagram\n- {図示|ずし}したように — as illustrated\n- {図示|ずし}した{結果|けっか} — the illustrated results\n\nUSAGE:\nPrimarily found in written academic and technical contexts. When authors want to reference a visual representation in a paper or report, they use {図示|ずし}する. In everyday language, {図|ず}で{示|しめ}す (to show with a diagram) is more natural.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {図解|ずかい} — illustrated explanation (the diagram itself, or the act of explaining with diagrams)\n- {表示|ひょうじ} — display, indication (broader, includes digital displays)",
